\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Worship the King, 
\par All glorious above;
\par O gratefully sing
\par His power and His love :
\par Our shield and defender,
\par The ancient of days,
\par Pavilioned in splendour,
\par And girded with praise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O tell of His might, 
\par O sing of His grace,
\par Whose robe is the light,
\par Whose canopy space;
\par His chariots of wrath 
\par The deep thunder-clouds from,
\par And dark is His path
\par On the wings of the storm.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The earth with its store 
\par Of wonders untold,
\par Almighty ! Thy power 
\par Hath founded of old,
\par Hath stablished it fast 
\par By a changeless decree,
\par And round it hath cast,
\par Like a mantle, the sea.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thy bountiful care 
\par What tongue can recite?
\par It breathes in the air,
\par It shines in the light,
\par It streams from the hills,
\par It descends to the plain,
\par And sweetly distils
\par In the dew and the rain. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Frail children of dust,
\par And feeble as frail,
\par In the do we trust,
\par Nor find Thee to fail;
\par Thy mercies how tender,
\par How firm to the end,
\par Our Maker, Defender,
\par Redeemer, and Friend !
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. O measureless Might !
\par Ineffable Love !
\par While angels delight 
\par To hymn Thee above,
\par The humbler creation,
\par Though feeble their lays,
\par With true adoration
\par Shall lisp to Thy praise.
\par                         Amen.
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

